  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 246 AM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nToday through mid-next week (Wednesday)...\n\nThrough this weekend: The Gulf Coast states remain entrenched\nunder a sprawling high at the surface and aloft (598 to 600DM).\nRAP analysis/water vapor imagery indicate the center of mid level \nhigh pressure remains over the Mid South to TN Valley region. This\npattern will gradually shift westward today into Friday, leading\nanomalous warmth, some 8-15F above normal (95F to 101F). Drier air\nis evident in GOES East total PWs (0.9 to 1.3 inches) and is\nprogged to shift into the region as the mid level high shifts\nwestward. While it will remain hot, dangerous heat stress will be\nsomewhat decreased. Lows will be seasonably warm, some 6-12F \nabove (70-75F this morning and a touch cooler tonight to the \nsouth, 67-70F along and south of I-20, while warmer to the north, \n71F-74F). \n\nHighs continue to moderate into the weekend, with an influx of \ndeeper moisture. A westward propagating upper low/surface trough \nover the northeast Gulf will lead to an influx of deeper moisture \naloft and higher boundary layer moisture, which supports less \nmixing and more concerns of dangerous heat. Highs will moderate \ninto the upper 90s to around 100F (97-102F), with 101-102F \npossible, especially in northern observation sites. Added some \ntargeted Limited heat graphics in the HWO for today into the \nweekend (along and northwest of the Natchez Trace today into \nFriday and areawide into the weekend). Holding off on any heat \nheadlines for now. Rain chances remain minimal, with some slight \nuptick in isolated/low chance rain and storm coverage in the Pine \nBelt late weekend on Sunday (15-30 percent).\n\nNext week (Through next Wednesday): As the upper low weakens and\nanother shortwave/cold core low propagates into the Mid West\nStates through middle of next week, the mid level feature over the\nnortheast Gulf is progged to lift northward. This feature will\nbecome absorbed in the mean flow to the north. This will lead to\nless focused moisture convergence but persistent deep moisture \n(PWs around 1.75 to greater than 2 inches). There is progged for \nanother weak frontal/convergence zone and light northwesterly flow\nto sink into the area early next week. Combined with the ridge \nless stout and centered over east TX, highs will become less \nseasonably warm, dropping from 8F to 14F above to 6F to 12F above\n(95F to 100F early week to 91F to 95F by midweek). Rain and storm\nchances remain in the low chance range (15-30 percent) on average\nareawide, with medium chance (exceeding 30 percent) in the Pine \nBelt. Dangerous heat concerns will persist into early week and \nwill continue to message HWO heat graphics for Monday and \nsomewhat less oppressive heat through midweek. /DC/",
